  <data name="S_InternalSettings" xml:space="preserve"><value>Insider settings</value></data><data name="C_EnableInternalSettings" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enable insider settings</value></data><data name="C_EnableInternalSettings_D" xml:space="preserve"><value>Temporarily shows insider attached settings.</value></data><data name="M_InternalSettings_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Insider settings enabled</value></data><data name="M_InternalSettings" xml:space="preserve"><value>Insider settings are now shown in the attached-settings menu for each student or prize on the list-management pages. This is active only for the current run and is hidden after restart.

Insider settings affect candidate weights and are not suitable for draws that need to be fair, public, or auditable. If a person with insider settings is selected, uploading the verification file may show a related notice and reveal that the settings were used.

Insider settings have lower priority than fair-draw rules. Selecting a student or prize with these settings does not guarantee a future selection.</value></data><data name="C_Enable" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enable</value></data>
